     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum daily dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. It carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis, and the risk is greater because this patient has no renal or hepatic issue that would explain a different plan. Once an order is in the system, it could be verified and given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a slip**, I can enter 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can also enter a lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals, if you want to titrate.\n- **If you intend a nonstandard dose**, please talk to the clinical pharmacist or the attending first. Then enter it through your hospital's high-alert or override process, with documented justification.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
